      "problem": "Consider the augmented matrix $M$ given by \n\n$$\nM=[\\begin{aligned}3 & -9 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 8\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nUse the standard method of Gaussian elimination to reduce $M$ to row echelon form.",
      "worked_solution": "Reducing $M$ to echelon form, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}M & =[\\begin{aligned}3 & -9 & 6 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & :=\\frac{1}{3}{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 4 & -12 & 8\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{2} & :={R}_{2}-4{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}1 & -3 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}].\\end{aligned}\n$$",
